course: dictionary
lesson: 3959
title: Furniture, a word with no plural
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Furniture means the big movable things in a room that make it useful, like tables, chairs, beds, sofas and wardrobes. You can see the meaning in the context: «Furniture and televisions that tip over injure many young children every year.» Tables and televisions are things that stand in a room, and when they tip over they can hurt people.
explain: Look at the words around furniture for clues. «Jumping on furniture can lead to falls and head bumps.» Jumping on a sofa or bed is not safe, so furniture is something you should not climb on. A safe room has its furniture fixed to the wall or placed where it cannot fall.
explain: Furniture is uncountable. You cannot say "a furniture" or "three furnitures". Instead, use a piece of furniture, or some furniture: "a piece of furniture" for one item and "pieces of furniture" for several. This is how we use the word in every sentence you read.
fact: Furniture means the large movable things in a room, like tables, chairs, beds, sofas and wardrobes.
fact: Furniture is an uncountable noun, so it has no plural: say "some furniture", not "furnitures".
fact: Use «a piece of furniture» to talk about one item, and «pieces of furniture» for more than one.
fact: «Furniture and televisions that tip over injure many young children every year.» Heavy furniture should be fixed to the wall so it cannot fall.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «garden furniture», «school furniture» and «rearrange the furniture».
exercise: «Furniture and televisions that tip over injure many young children every year.» What is furniture? | *The large movable things in a room, like tables and beds | Food kept in a cupboard | Small things you wear on your hands | Rooms in a house, such as the kitchen
exercise: Which of these is a piece of furniture? | Cloud | Bread | *Wardrobe | Puddle
exercise: Ruby says, «I bought three furnitures for my room.» What is wrong with her sentence? | She should say three televisions instead | She should use the word furnish instead | Nothing, furnitures is a correct plural | *Furniture has no plural, so she should say three pieces of furniture
test: «Jumping on furniture can lead to falls and head bumps.» What should you not do, according to this sentence? | Clear space around you | Sit quietly on a chair | Fix a bookcase to the wall | *Jump on furniture
test: Mia wants to rearrange the furniture in her bedroom. What is she going to do? | Water the plants on the windowsill | *Move the beds, tables and chairs to new places | Paint the ceiling blue | Eat her lunch on the floor
exam: «For motion games, clear space around you so you do not hit furniture or people.» Why should you clear space before a motion game? | *So you do not bump into furniture or people | So the controller can fly across the room | To make the room look bigger for guests | To make the game easier to win
